<title>UK: BADMINTON-WORLD INDIVIDUAL CHAMPIONSHIP MEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-WORLD INDIVIDUAL CHAMPIONSHIP MEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>GLASGOW 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of men's matches at the world individual badminton championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>1-Dong Jiong (China) beat Jang Chun-woong (South Korea) 15-6</p>
<p>15-3</p>
<p>10-Thomas Stuer-Lauridsen (Denmark) beat Thomas Johansson</p>
<p>(Sweden) 15-3 18-15</p>
<p>Jeroen Van Dijk (Netherlands) beat Andrej Pohar (Slovenia) 15-1</p>
<p>15-6</p>
<p>6-Ong Ewe Hock (Malaysia) beat Vladislav Druzchenko (Ukraine)</p>
<p>13-18 15-4 15-12</p>
<p>Darren Hall (England) beat Bruce Flockhart (Scotland) 15-4</p>
<p>15-11</p>
<p>12-Heryanto Arbi (Indonesia) beat Juergen Koch (Austria) 15-1</p>
<p>15-6</p>
<p>Mike Breres (Canada) beat Chien Yu-hsiu (Taiwan) 15-9 15-13</p>
<p>Kevin Han (U.S.) beat Oliver Pongratz (Germany), walkover</p>
<p>Fernando Silva (Portugal) beat Gopichand (India), walkover</p>
<p>men's singles first round results</p>
<p>Pavel Uvarov (Russia) beat Detlef Poste (Germany) 18-13 12-15 15-12</p>
<p>4-Indra Wijaya (Indonesia) beat Pontus Jantti (Finland) 15-3</p>
<p>4-15 15-11</p>
<p>Mark Constable (England) beat Tam Lok Tin (Hong Kong) 3-15 15-9 15-10</p>
<p>15-Peter Rasmussen (Denmark) beat Apichai Thiraratsakul (Thailand) 15-7 15-6</p>
<p>Lin Liwen (China) beat Michael Korchouk (Belarus)  15-5 15-1</p>
<p>8-Park Sung-woo (South Korea) beat Muhammed Saqib Majeed (Pakistan) 15-6 15-8</p>
<p>Dicky Palyama (Netherlands) beat Keita Masuda (Japan) 15-9 11-15 15-11</p>
<p>13-Allan Budi Kusama (Indonesia) beatVikrant Patwardhan (India) 15-8 15-1</p>
<p>Henrik Bengtsson (Sweden) beat Marco Vasconcelos (Portugal) 15-1 15-7</p>
</text>
